wifi: mt76: mt7603: initialize global station WCID

mt7603 uses a driver-private global station WCID for frames that have
neither a station nor a vif, including frames injected through a monitor
interface. Unlike the core global WCID initialized by
mt76_register_device(), this WCID is published without ever being passed
to mt76_wcid_init().

mt76_tx() queues every such frame on the WCID's tx_pending queue and links
its tx_list. The first injected frame therefore reaches
__skb_queue_tail() with an uninitialized sk_buff_head and dereferences a
NULL prev pointer, which on MT7628 (Mi Router 4C) panics the kernel and
reboots the board.

Initialize the WCID before publishing it.

Backport of upstream commit c50f17ec046e ("wifi: mt76: mt7603:
initialize global station WCID") to mt76 as pinned by OpenWrt 23.05.5
(1e336a8582dce2ef32ddd440d423e9afef961e71). On that version
mt76_wcid_init() still takes a single argument.

--- a/mt7603/init.c
+++ b/mt7603/init.c
@@ -229,6 +229,7 @@
 
 	eth_broadcast_addr(bc_addr);
 	mt7603_wtbl_init(dev, MT7603_WTBL_RESERVED, -1, bc_addr);
+	mt76_wcid_init(&dev->global_sta.wcid);
 	dev->global_sta.wcid.idx = MT7603_WTBL_RESERVED;
 	rcu_assign_pointer(dev->mt76.wcid[MT7603_WTBL_RESERVED],
 			   &dev->global_sta.wcid);
